    "result_text": "Done. All tests pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests green \u2014 the full suite).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented structured address support for owners while keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n**Contract (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`)** \u2014 added `addressLine1` (optional, non-blank when supplied) and `addressLine2` (optional) to the `OwnerFields` schema, and removed `address` from the required list so a structured-only owner is valid. The `address` field is documented as the composed/legacy line.\n\n**Entity + schema** \u2014 added `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` columns to `Owner` (`address_line1`, `address_line2`) and to all four `db/*/schema.sql` files so they persist and round-trip through `GET`.\n\n**New helper `OwnerAddress`** \u2014 the single place that reconciles the two forms:\n- `normalizeInPlace(...)` normalizes whichever address fields are supplied (via the existing `AddressNormalizer`: upper-case, collapse whitespace, expand `ST\u2192STREET`), then sets the flat `address` to the composed line \u2014 normalized `addressLine1`, plus a single space and normalized `addressLine2` when present. Structured fields win when `addressLine1` is present; otherwise the normalized flat `address` stands.\n- `hasAddress(...)` enforces validity: a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address`.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `RequireOwnerFields` (POST first step) now calls `OwnerAddress.normalizeInPlace` and checks `hasAddress` for the either-or rule; `ApplyOwner` (PUT) does the same and copies the structured lines. `BuildOwner`/MapStruct map the new fields by name automatically.\n\nBecause `city` and `postcode` are shared across both address forms, the household hash, postcode validation, and locality already read them unchanged \u2014 they keep working identically whichever form is used.\n\nTest results from `structuredOwner()` with `addressLine1=\"10 king st\"`: `GET` returns `addressLine1=\"10 KING STREET\"` and composed `address=\"10 KING STREET\"`; the flat-address path still returns 2xx.",
